cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RabMV, please cite it as below."
title: "RabMV: Registry-Aware Boosting Machine of Valledupar"
abstract: >-
  An explainable boosting machine (a generalized additive model fitted by cyclic Newton boosting) that knows
  the structure of the public-health registry its data come from: which concepts each surveillance form
  measures, in which version and how comparably. It declares the registry in TOML files, audits undeclared
  differential measurement between forms, admits a concept only when both classes measured it comparably, and
  marginalizes what a form did not measure, with purified pairwise interactions.
